<p>I work primarily on planetary astrophysics. Current topics of interest aim to understand how the diverse array of planetary systems formed and continue to evolve, particularly as revealed by the structure of circumstellar disks which we can now image in great detail. I am also interested the processes by which massive stars eject dust towards the end of their evolution and replenish material in their neighbourhood, which may go on to form and influence a new generation of stars and planets. You are welcome to <a href="./science">read more</a> about these topics.</p>

